cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or build upon its ideas in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "MaoField: A Dialectical-Materialist Framework for Non-Statistical Semantic Representation"
abstract: >-
  MaoField is a computational framework grounded in dialectical materialism and
  realized through partial differential equations describing semantic field
  evolution. It axiomatizes seven foundational principles, formalizes them via
  category-theoretic adjunctions (Lawvere 1970), and implements them using
  coupled Allen-Cahn and complex Ginzburg-Landau dynamics. Initial experiments
  on five BEIR benchmarks show that PDE-based field evolution extracts
  semantic signal from raw byte sources (nDCG@10 gains of 48-172% over byte
  baselines at top-20 reranking). Attractor-capacity analysis reveals a
  fundamental bound: under double-well Ginzburg-Landau potentials, the system
  admits only k*≈2 stable attractors via source-density-coupled symmetry
  regimes (Z_1 phase collapse for byte sources; Z_2 amplitude bistability for
  learned embeddings). This is a direction-setting proposal inviting
  cross-disciplinary collaboration.
